{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: recover the undelivered host wake-up and watcher outcome of withdrawn #2807. Keep current full Tailapp I7 and batch-review follow-through first; queue this after the existing Gitseq work through #20827, and state the actual queue position or a concrete availability constraint. This is distinct from MCP review assurance.\n\n#2807 asked for a checked Codex/Claude host capability matrix, a portable actor-targeted watcher, and a real supported wake/resume integration if available. Its author retirement #7103 instead said the two-screen UI redesign removed the target and that addressed wait/ack delivery landed the substance. [The original request and retirement](host-wakeup-recovery.json) show that the host outcome was not a browser-screen outcome. Adopted UI proposal #6730 describes list/thread navigation and does not disposition host wake-up.\n\nCurrent [wait documentation](docs/reference/mcp/wait.md@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:118) still states the boundary explicitly: it can return chat to a running waiter, but cannot start or wake an idle agent host. The current [MCP dispatch](cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:1191) delivers actor-wait results; it is not proof a host schedules a model. Current source and request searches found no later matrix, local watcher delivery or supported-host proof. Confirm the then-current implementation before duplicating anything. Do not infer that a silent but live native process is stopped or that a host lacks an API merely because our MCP client has not called it.\n\nRecover the complete original outcome on current interfaces. Verify the command-line and desktop hosts actually used here and the applicable current MCP subscription/extension contract, using local documented capabilities first and authoritative vendor/protocol sources where needed. Distinguish protocol receipt, host notification, existing-task resume and model invocation. For each host, record the tested version, supported API or explicit absence, opt-in/setup, and observed result. Do not freeze the historical protocol date or substitute deprecated logging/sampling for delivery.\n\nSpecify and deliver one small testable actor-targeted watch seam over existing recipient-aware inbox semantics: exact actor, text, about anchor, conversation/sequence, reply target and priority reason. Prefer a declared supported subscription/extension; provide the same semantics through a documented long-running local watcher/NDJSON interface when that is the portable fallback. Demonstrate at least one real wake/resume integration if a supported authorized API is available. Otherwise deliver the ratifiable boundary/spike artifact naming the smallest host change needed AND the testable watcher seam; documentation saying “the host must wake itself” alone does not satisfy the request.\n\nPreserve exact actor/thread routing, dedupe and coalescing across sessions, bounded storms/rate limits, quiet/off, disconnect/reconnect and expiry. Resumed context identifies priority ephemeral chat and its authenticated provenance, prompts inspection before routine work where appropriate, and makes clear that chat does not create a durable assignment or grant authority. No sender impersonation, automatic promise, wrong-actor wake, indefinite conversation retention or trust elevation of message text.\n\nThis is source/design and controlled integration proof, not permission to install an unattended production agent or alter live user sessions. Use supported opt-in test fixtures and respect existing approvals; terminal-control review rejection must not be retried through another route. If an actual host test needs unavailable explicit permission, preserve that condition as a concrete blocker on the promise and complete independent design/seam work. Do not declare a host unsupported merely to avoid an available integration requirement.\n\nThe current wait-page artifact is live with ordinary inherited staleness and is byte-identical to current main. The effective author retirement is retained as recovery history. Reconcile current bases at intake, preserve the original full outcome and the UI decision, and keep corrections on the same live commitment.","body":{"branch":"request/ephemeral-host-wakeup-recovery","conditions":"On request/ephemeral-host-wakeup-recovery from then-current main: a checked, dated matrix covers the actual Codex and Claude CLI/desktop hosts and distinguishes MCP receipt, notifications, task resume and model invocation. Deliver one tested portable actor-targeted watch contract/seam; demonstrate a real supported opt-in host integration when available, otherwise a ratifiable boundary/spike naming the missing capability plus the working local watcher. Cover exact routing, session coalescing/dedupe, rate bounds/storms, quiet/off, reconnect, expiry, no wrong-actor wake, no impersonation/automatic promises and priority-context trust/authority labels. Exercise real process boundaries and positive/negative controls; a mocked notification or returned tool response is not proof of model wake-up. A permission dependency remains explicit and does not excuse independent work or silently erase required integration. Preserve existing recipient inbox/wait/ack semantics and UI policy. Update affected architecture and setup/reference documentation at the same head with honest supported/polling-only/unsupported classifications and current source bases. Run proportionate relevant tests plus required repository checks, publish exact-path reporting artifacts, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the verdict, seal to main with exact-path succession, push source and sequence, verify CI and delete owned worktrees/branches. If a design-only stage needs to land separately, file a child before that landing and keep the full recovery outcome live. No production agent/service installation, key changes, live-session manipulation, or approval bypass. Keep full I7 and batch follow-through intact; queue after existing work through20827.","head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d2bf2b6a1fad0bc51cb43e2368ec2824dc125ae1 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02320b2eaa39a0ec7e47f31205c4b25afa46609f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03bf9ae04ffa1aadb0f8f5018e3936c2bb72576e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:05fc291d6b04e1040f1357b91b0c32a9a7cef699, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0fae00055767520da097d824d3f7732892d47ef8 and 47 more","target_head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}